    <div class="og-bench-copy">
      <p class="og-walk-eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h2 id="og-faq-title">Questions, answered.</h2>
      <p>Common questions about hosting OpenGeocode, what it costs, and how accurate it is.</p>
      <a class="og-bench-link" href="/docs/">Read the documentation</a>
    </div>
    <div class="og-faq-list">
      <details>
        <summary>How do I use OpenGeocode?</summary>
        <p>Build a Pack with <code>og build</code>, then <code>og serve</code> it. See the <a href="/docs/quickstart/">quickstart</a>.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What hardware do I need to host it?</summary>
        <p>Very little. This page's search serves the whole planet, a 26.3&nbsp;GB Pack, from a 4&nbsp;vCPU VM with 7.6&nbsp;GB of RAM, using about 0.5&nbsp;GB of memory.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How much does OpenGeocode cost?</summary>
        <p>Nothing. No API key, quota or per-lookup fee; you only pay for your machine.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does it work offline?</summary>
        <p>Yes. It only needs a connection to download data when building a Pack.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I geocode a whole CSV?</summary>
        <p>Yes, with <code>open-geocode geocode batch</code>. See <a href="/docs/guides/batch-csv/">batch geocoding</a>.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How accurate is it?</summary>
        <p>It leads the open-source geocoders on the MESSY STREETS benchmark. See the <a href="/docs/benchmarks/">benchmarks</a>.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What about data and privacy?</summary>
        <p>It runs on your hardware, so no address leaves your network.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is OpenGeocode open source?</summary>
        <p>Yes, MIT-licensed, on <a href="https://github.com/open-geocode-rs/open-geocode">GitHub</a>.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
